{
  "schema": "devine-bms-device-template/0",
  "id": "mitsubishi-bac-hd150-group",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "hardwareId": "H6",
  "vendor": "Mitsubishi Electric",
  "model": "BAC-HD150 (one group)",
  "dis": "One indoor-unit group on a Mitsubishi BAC-HD150 BACnet gateway (M-NET 1). Repeat per group with step 100.",
  "status": "datasheet only",
  "protocols": [
    "bacnet_ip"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Object instances are MM GG NN: M-NET number, group number, member number. This template is M-NET 1 with group 00; bulk create with repeat from the first group to the last and step 100 (group 5 member 09 is 010509).",
    "Mode and fan speed are read as state numbers. The order of the states (Cool, Heat, Fan, Auto, Dry; Low, High, Mid) is not given in the pages read; check each object's state-text on the bench, then change these points to Str with an enum list.",
    "Error codes are coarse categories (1 normal to 9 system error); the detailed fault code is only on the Mitsubishi side.",
    "Set temperature ranges depend on the model and mode (standard indoor unit: cooling 19 to 30, heating 17 to 28 °C); set write limits to match when commands arrive (milestone 7).",
    "After a power cut the gateway takes up to 10 minutes before BACnet is ready; expect these points to be down for that long.",
    "COV is switched on per object in the Mitsubishi Setting Tool; leave the device's cov off unless that is done."
  ],
